      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm prepping for the upcoming trade summit in Jakarta. I want to use a local idiom in my opening remarks to show I've done my homework and to build some quick rapport with the ministers. I was thinking of using the phrase \"makan hati\" to describe the intensity of our negotiations. Is that considered a safe, neutral way to show familiarity, or is it sensitive?",
